        <senderName>NWS San Juan PR</senderName>
        <headline>Marine Weather Statement issued August 2 at 3:43PM AST by NWS San Juan PR</headline>
        <description>The areas affected include...
Atlantic Waters of Puerto Rico AND USVI from 10 NM to 19.5N...
Coastal Waters of Northern Puerto Rico out 10 NM...
Mona Passage Southward to 17N...

At 341 PM AST, Doppler radar indicated a strong thunderstorm, capable
of producing winds to around 30 knots. This thunderstorm was located
over the waters nearly 15 nautical miles northwest of Aguadilla,
moving northwest at 15 knots.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners can expect gusty winds to around 30 knots, locally higher
waves, lightning strikes, and heavy downpours. Boaters should seek
safe harbor immediately until this storm passes.</instruction>
