            <value>SPS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>SPS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-08-02T13:59:00-06:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-08-02T13:59:00-06:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-02T14:30:00-06:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Pueblo CO</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 2 at 1:59PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO</headline>
        <description>At 159 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over
southeastern Colorado Springs, moving east at 35 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Colorado Springs, Air Force Academy, Ellicott, Schriever Space Force
Base, Falcon, Cimarron Hills, Peterson Space Force Base, Stratmoor,
and Security-Widefield.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SPSPUB</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>WMOidentifier</valueName>
            <value>WWUS85 KPUB 021959</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>NWSheadline</valueName>
            <value>A STRONG THUNDERSTORM WILL IMPACT CENTRAL EL PASO COUNTY THROUGH 230 PM MDT</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>eventMotionDescription</valueName>
            <value>2025-08-02T19:59:00-00:00...storm...279DEG...30KT...38.85,-104.72</value>
        </parameter>
