        <expires>2025-08-02T14:45:00-06:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa NM</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 2 at 2:13PM MDT by NWS El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa NM</headline>
        <description>At 212 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over
Bear Canyon, moving southwest at 10 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and nickel size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Ruidoso, Lake Mescalero, Snow Canyon, Fence Canyon, Portions of US
Highway 70 between Apache Summit and the Otero-Lincoln County Line,
Bear Canyon, and Whitetail.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead to
localized flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SPSEPZ</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>WMOidentifier</valueName>
            <value>WWUS84 KEPZ 022013</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>NWSheadline</valueName>
            <value>A STRONG THUNDERSTORM WILL IMPACT NORTH CENTRAL OTERO COUNTY THROUGH 245 PM MDT</value>
