        <senderName>NWS Riverton WY</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 2 at 3:05PM MDT by NWS Riverton WY</headline>
        <description>At 304 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over
Hamilton Dome, which is 17 miles northwest of Thermopolis, moving
east at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could blow around unsecured objects. Minor hail
damage to vegetation is possible.

This storm will remain over mainly rural areas of central Hot Springs
County, including the following locations... Hot Springs County
Airport.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
