        <senderName>NWS San Angelo TX</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 2 at 4:05PM CDT by NWS San Angelo TX</headline>
        <description>At 405 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near
I-10 Near The Crockett-Sutton County Line, or 16 miles northwest of
Sonora, moving slowly south at 5 to 10 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
I-10 Near The Crockett-Sutton County Line and The Intersection Of
I-10 And Ranch Road 1989.

This includes Interstate 10 between Mile Markers 379 and 395.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
