        <senderName>NWS Tallahassee FL</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 3 at 11:27AM EDT by NWS Tallahassee FL</headline>
        <description>At 1127 AM EDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over
Havana, moving northeast at 20 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Tallahassee, Tallahassee State College, Florida State University,
Midway, Havana, Florida A and M, Doak Campbell Stadium, Lake
Bradford, Gaither Community Center, Tallahassee Memorial Hosp, Walker
Ford Community Center, Jamieson, Rocky Hill, South City, Griffin
Heights, Calvary, Tallahassee Regional A/P, Governors Square Mall,
Midtown, and Apalachee Ridge Estates.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead to
localized flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.

Frequent cloud to ground lightning is occurring with this storm.
Lightning can strike 10 miles away from a thunderstorm. Seek a safe
shelter inside a building or vehicle.</instruction>
