        <senderName>NWS Indianapolis IN</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 5 at 8:24PM EDT by NWS Indianapolis IN</headline>
        <description>At 824 PM EDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 10
miles north of North Vernon, or 14 miles east of Columbus, moving
north at 5 mph.

HAZARD...Winds in excess of 40 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Westport and Letts.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
