        <senderName>NWS Peachtree City GA</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 5 at 8:32PM EDT by NWS Peachtree City GA</headline>
        <description>At 832 PM EDT, a strong thunderstorm was near Sand Hill, or 7 miles
northwest of Cusseta, moving east at 10 mph.

HAZARD...Heavy rain.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Heavy rain may cause temporary street flooding especially
in poor drainage areas.

Locations impacted include...
Cusseta, North Fort Benning, Saint Marys Hills, Highland Park,
Christopher, Sand Hill, Battle Park, Vista Terrace, Manta, Kenwood,
Custer Road Terrace, Jamestown/South Fort Benning, Eelbeck/West Fort
Benning, Benning Hills, Benning Park, Carter Acres, Edgewood, and
Avondale.
</description>
        <instruction>Motorists should slow down and be prepared for possible loss of
control due to hydroplaning.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
