        <senderName>NWS Lubbock TX</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 5 at 7:52PM CDT by NWS Lubbock TX</headline>
        <description>At 751 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over
Enochs, or 10 miles north of Morton, moving northeast at 5 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph and half inch hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Enochs, Bula, and Muleshoe Wildlife Refuge.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Heavy rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead to
localized flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
