    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>Special Weather Statement</event>
        <responseType>Execute</responseType>
        <urgency>Expected</urgency>
        <severity>Moderate</severity>
        <certainty>Observed</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>SPS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>SPS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-08-05T20:07:00-05:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-08-05T20:07:00-05:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-05T20:45:00-05:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Grand Forks ND</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 5 at 8:07PM CDT by NWS Grand Forks ND</headline>
        <description>At 806 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking strong thunderstorms along
a line extending from near Lisbon to near Rutland to near Havana.
Movement was east at 25 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph and half inch hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Lisbon, Enderlin, Gwinner, Milnor, Lidgerwood, Forman, and Wyndmere.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with these storms and may lead
to localized flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
